entries.body:
Normality —

N. normality, normalcy, normalness†; familiarity, naturalness; commonness ; rule, standard ; customary ; standard, pattern .

V. normalize, standardize. Adj. normal, natural, unexceptional; common, usual ;

Incredulity — N. incredulousness†, incredulity; skepticism, pyrrhonism†; want of faith &c.†. suspiciousness &c. adj.; scrupulosity; suspicion &c.. mistrust, cynicism. unbeliever, skeptic, cynic; misbeliever.1, pyrrhonist; heretic &c..

V. be incredulous &c. adj.; distrust &c.; refuse to believe; shut one's eyes to, shut one's ears to; turn a deaf ear to; hold aloof, ignore, nullis jurare in verba magistri .

Adj. incredulous, skeptical, unbelieving, inconvincible†; hard of belief, shy of belief, disposed to doubt, indisposed to believe; suspicious, scrupulous, distrustful, cynical;
